## Original Content
When Twitch announced that streamers could opt out, thousands of users questioned why their content was being used to train AI models in the first place.

## Summary
Twitch has introduced an opt-out feature allowing streamers to prevent their content from being used to train Amazon's AI models. The announcement led to widespread user questioning about the initial lack of consent for data utilization. This highlights ongoing concerns about data privacy and AI ethics in tech platforms.

## Key Points
- Twitch implemented an opt-out mechanism for streamers to exclude their content from AI training.
- The move sparked controversy as thousands of users questioned why their data was used without prior consent.
- It underscores issues of transparency and user rights in AI development processes.
- Users are demanding greater control over personal data usage by companies like Amazon.


